  "voiceover": "You are not the first person to ask. The hardest question you have about the Christian faith is almost certainly older than you think. Open Matthew's Gospel, chapter 28, and the earliest answer his opponents gave is already written down — his disciples came by night and stole him away, while we were asleep. Sleeping men, testifying to what happened while they slept. The church did not hide that. It wrote it down. Around AD 160 Justin Martyr names the same charge, still in circulation, generations later. Around 248 Origen answers the philosopher Celsus — who had written seventy years earlier — point by point, in writing. Twenty centuries, and the pattern never changes. Every generation brings its hardest question. Every generation answers. This faith has never needed the question not to be asked. That is what Asked and Answered is: a hundred and two questions, answered plainly, and reviewed before they were published. Bring the question you have been carrying. It has been asked before, and it has an answer.",
